      "Notes",
      "The Townsend index is a measure of material deprivation within a population. The index uses four variables derived from census data:\n\u2022\tPercentage unemployment (of those aged 16 and over who are economically active)\n\u2022\tPercentage overcrowded households (of all households)\n\u2022\tPercentage no car/vans ownership (of all households)\nThe Townsend index is created by summing z-scores of logged unemployment, logged overcrowding, no car, and renters.\n\u2022\tPercentage non-home owners (of all households)"
    ]
